<section class="view" id="home"><div class="hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">Independent designer · Available for select projects</div><h1>Make it useful.<br><em>Make it human.</em></h1><p>I'm Alex Morgan, a product designer and front-end developer turning complex ideas into clear, thoughtful digital experiences.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="#work">Explore selected work</a><a class="btn ghost" href="#contact">Let's talk</a></div><div class="social" style="margin-top:28px"><span>Product design</span><span>·</span><span>UI engineering</span><span>·</span><span>Design systems</span></div></div><div class="portrait" role="img" aria-label="Illustrated portrait placeholder"><div class="portrait-label">Thoughtful digital craft, from idea to launch.</div></div></div><div class="wrap" style="padding-top:0"><div class="grid"><div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">01 / Strategy</div><h3>Start with people</h3><p>Research and clear problem framing create better foundations.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">02 / Design</div><h3>Find the signal</h3><p>Simple, accessible interfaces make difficult things feel easy.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">03 / Build</div><h3>Make it real</h3><p>Close collaboration helps good ideas become great products.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="view" id="about"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">A little about me</div><h1 class="section-title">Curiosity is part of the process.</h1><div class="two"><div><p class="sub">I partner with ambitious teams to make useful, accessible products. My work spans early discovery, interaction design, prototyping, and front-end implementation—always with a focus on the people using what we make.</p><p class="sub">Over the past eight years I've helped early-stage teams find product clarity and helped established organizations modernize the experiences their customers rely on.</p><p class="sub">When I’m not making things for screens, you'll probably find me sketching in a café, exploring a new city, or tending an unruly collection of houseplants.</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">What I bring</div><h2 class="section-title">Good questions. Clear systems.</h2><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Product strategy</span><span class="tag">UX research</span><span class="tag">Interaction design</span><span class="tag">Design systems</span><span class="tag">HTML & CSS</span><span class="tag">JavaScript</span><span class="tag">Accessibility</span><span class="tag">Prototyping</span></div><blockquote class="quote">“Alex brings calm, clarity, and a rare ability to connect the details to the bigger picture.”</blockquote><div class="meta">— Jordan Lee, product lead</div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="view" id="work"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Selected projects · 2022–2026</div><h1 class="section-title">A few things I've helped make.</h1><p class="sub">A selection of product and design work. Project links are illustrative for this portfolio demonstration.</p><div class="grid"><article class="card"><div class="project-art">FIELDNOTES</div><div class="eyebrow">Product design · SaaS</div><h3>Fieldnotes, reimagined</h3><p>Helped a research team move from scattered documents to one clear, collaborative workspace.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Discovery</span><span class="tag">Prototyping</span><span class="tag">Design system</span></div><p><a class="social" href="#contact">Discuss this project →</a></p></article><article class="card"><div class="project-art">NORTH / SOUTH</div><div class="eyebrow">UX & engineering · Commerce</div><h3>A calmer way to shop</h3><p>Simplified a mobile checkout and made product information easier to compare.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Mobile UX</span><span class="tag">Accessibility</span><span class="tag">Frontend</span></div><p><a class="social" href="#contact">Discuss this project →</a></p></article><article class="card"><div class="project-art">COMMON GROUND</div><div class="eyebrow">Strategy · Community</div><h3>Finding local connection</h3><p>Designed a service that helps neighbors discover volunteer events and shared resources.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Service design</span><span class="tag">Research</span><span class="tag">Web app</span></div><p><a class="social" href="#contact">Discuss this project →</a></p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="view" id="resume"><div class="wrap"><div class="resume-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Experience, education & skills</div><h1 class="section-title">The short version.</h1></div><button id="downloadResume">Download resume</button></div><div class="two"><div class="panel"><h2>Experience</h2><div class="timeline"><div class="milestone"><small>2022 — Present</small><h3>Independent product designer & developer</h3><p class="sub">Partnering with product teams on research, strategy, design systems, and frontend delivery.</p></div><div class="milestone"><small>2019 — 2022</small><h3>Senior product designer · Northstar Studio</h3><p class="sub">Led end-to-end product design for early-stage technology and public-service clients.</p></div><div class="milestone"><small>2017 — 2019</small><h3>UX designer · Brightside Digital</h3><p class="sub">Designed customer-facing experiences and contributed to a shared component library.</p></div></div></div><div class="panel"><h2>Education & capabilities</h2><p><b>B.Des. Interaction Design</b><br><span class="sub">Coastal Institute of Design · 2017</span></p><div class="resume-block"><b>Design</b><p class="sub">Research · UX strategy · Prototyping · Visual design · Accessibility</p></div><div class="resume-block"><b>Development</b><p class="sub">Semantic HTML · CSS · JavaScript · Responsive interfaces · Design systems</p></div><div class="resume-block"><b>Languages</b><p class="sub">English · Spanish</p></div></div></div><p class="meta">Demo resume details are fictional and can be edited directly in this HTML file.</p></div></section>
<section class="view" id="journal"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Notes on making things</div><h1 class="section-title">A work in progress, by nature.</h1><div class="grid"><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Design systems · 5 min</div><h3>Consistency is a team sport</h3><p class="sub">A design system works best when the people using it help shape it.</p><a class="social" href="#contact">Let's compare notes →</a></article><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Accessibility · 7 min</div><h3>The small details are the experience</h3><p class="sub">Accessible defaults are a practical way to make everyday interfaces work for more people.</p><a class="social" href="#contact">Let's compare notes →</a></article><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Process · 4 min</div><h3>Prototype the question, not the answer</h3><p class="sub">A lightweight experiment can make the next decision much easier.</p><a class="social" href="#contact">Let's compare notes →</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="view" id="contact"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Have a good challenge in mind?</div><h1 class="section-title">Let's make something matter.</h1><div class="two"><div><p class="sub">I'm currently available for a small number of new projects, collaborations, and conversations.</p><div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">Get in touch</div><p><a class="social" href="mailto:hello@alexmorgan.example">hello@alexmorgan.example</a></p><p class="social"><a href="#work">LinkedIn</a><a href="#work">Dribbble</a><a href="#work">GitHub</a></p><p class="meta">Social links are illustrative demo destinations.</p></div></div><form id="contactForm" class="panel"><label>Your name<input class="field" name="name" autocomplete="name" required></label><label>Email address<input class="field" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required></label><label>What are you working on?<textarea class="field" name="message" rows="5" required></textarea></label><button>Send an inquiry</button><p class="status" id="contactStatus" role="status"></p><p class="meta">This demo form shows a local confirmation; it does not send your details to a server.</p></form></div></div></section>
